From 803949750d16e120602ab507e9c69ef04f3d357e Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Nex <63727521+LuCiLuna@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Mon, 2 Nov 2026 00:27:28 -0600
Subject: [PATCH 110/114] Input: add the OnePlus alert slider

A magnet moves between two IST8801 hall sensors, and the difference between
their readings gives the position. On the OnePlus 9 Pro that reads about +105,
0 and -105, with about 10 of noise, so fixed thresholds do the job without the
vendor's per-phone calibration. Report it as ABS_MISC so userspace can read the
position at any time.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
---
 .../boot/dts/qcom/sm8350-oneplus-common.dtsi  |  21 +-
 drivers/input/misc/Kconfig                    |  11 +
 drivers/input/misc/Makefile                   |   1 +
 drivers/input/misc/oneplus-alert-slider.c     | 364 ++++++++++++++++++
 4 files changed, 396 insertions(+), 1 deletion(-)
 create mode 100644 drivers/input/misc/oneplus-alert-slider.c

